    "show_share": true,
    "description": "The Aga Khan University, Faculty of Arts & Sciences (AKU-FAS) celebrated the launch of  Psychoanalytic Sociology: A New Theory of the Social Bond , the latest work from Dr Duane Rousselle, Associate Dean and Professor at AKU-FAS. This new book challenges traditional concepts of social bonds, urging readers to reconsider how we connect in a world that feels increasingly divided. Dr Rousselle's exploration delves into a question that resonates deeply today: \"How can we relate to others?\" in a time marked by 'social narcissism'. This self-centred approach, he argues, weakens collective bonds as individuals prioritize personal satisfaction over communal ties. He contends that as digital immersion intensifies, even social theorists must now grapple with the blurred boundaries between private and public spaces brought about by social media - a transformation he warns diminishes the 'sociological imagination' by eroding its critical lens.",
